# Section title typography

Use these sizes consistently for marketing/content sections (not the hero H1).

## Section headers (`h2`)

Examples: “About Our Web Development Services”, “Our Process”, “Why Choose Us”, “What We Build”, “Industries We Serve”.

- **Font size:** `36px` → Tailwind `text-[36px]`
- **Font weight:** `700` → Tailwind `font-bold`
- Prefer: `text-[36px] font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight`
- Do **not** use responsive title stacks like `text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl` for these section headers unless the user explicitly asks

Prefer `SectionHeading` when the title/subtitle come from i18n keys.

## Body / supporting text

Paragraphs in about blocks, card descriptions, and section subtitles:

- **Font size:** `16px` → Tailwind `text-base`
- Do not bump body copy to `text-lg` / `md:text-lg` by default

## Card titles (`h3`)

Keep card titles smaller than section headers (typically `text-base` / `font-semibold`). Do not make card titles `36px`.

## Heroes

Page heroes (home `Hero`, `ServiceHero`) may use larger display sizes. This rule applies to **section** headers below the hero, not the hero H1.
